# Optional build-time default for the console's Bearer credential. Prefer
# entering a token at runtime: the console prompts after a 401 and Settings
# offers a "switch credential" control, keeping the token in sessionStorage
# for one tab and out of the bundle. VITE_API_TOKEN is inlined into the public
# JavaScript bundle at build time, so anyone who can load the console can
# extract it. Use it only on trusted networks; production deployments should
# use OIDC or managed user credentials instead (leave VITE_API_TOKEN unset).
# For controlled Docker builds pass it explicitly:
#   docker build --build-arg VITE_API_TOKEN=... .
#
# Must match the Hub's ARKFLOW_OPERATOR_TOKEN (or a managed `ark_...`
# credential) when operator authentication is enabled.
# VITE_API_TOKEN=operator-secret
# Optional; defaults to the Vite proxy path.
# VITE_API_BASE=/api/v1
